  "requirement": "A definition glob MUST match a complete full name. `*` MUST match zero or more characters, including dots; all other valid name characters MUST match literally. An empty glob MUST be invalid. Every definition selection MUST use this matching rule, including requirements evidence inputs, CLI definition filters, and the authoring `references` tool, and MUST match against both requirements and named examples.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no gap. `definition_glob::matches` and `definition_glob::validate` (`src/definition_glob.rs`) carry out the matching rule and the empty-glob and invalid-character checks. Each selection path I read applies that rule to requirements and named examples and skips terms. Those paths are evidence inputs (`InputSelector::resolve` in `src/inputs.rs` and `source_input` in `src/authoring/inputs.rs`), the CLI `status` and `info` filters (`src/commands.rs`), and the authoring `references` and `referencing` code (`src/authoring/tools.rs`). A search of `src` found no other glob matcher.\n\nTests cover the obligations:\n- **Matching rule:** the unit test in `src/definition_glob.rs` covers `*` crossing dots, whole-name matching, and invalid and empty globs. `tests/commands.rs` covers `requirements.*ready`, which exercises `*` matching zero characters.\n- **Evidence inputs:** the evidence test in `src/evidence.rs`, `tests/definitions.rs` and the `requirements_reads...` test cover requirements and examples being selected, named definitions being excluded, and invalid or empty globs being rejected.\n- **CLI filters:** `tests/commands.rs` and `tests/definitions.rs` cover invalid globs, unmatched selections, and selection of requirements and examples.\n- **Authoring tools:** the `references` and `referencing` tests in `src/authoring/tools.rs` cover `\"\"` and `bad name` being rejected and unmatched globs being reported.\n\nNo `{fixme}` references apply. `disagreements` in `src/commands.rs` calls the shared matcher without its own `{impl}` reference, but it only calls the shared matcher, so I did not treat it as a gap.",
